---
description:
  Verifies that, under the ELK layout engine, a subgraph's title text width is
  reserved before edge routing when the title is wider than every child node it
  contains, so that edges terminate at the subgraph's painted border rather than
  ending inside it, and the frame is not resized after the fact.
config:
  layout: elk
---
%% Every subgraph title here is wider than the nodes inside it. ELK must reserve
%% the title width before routing, so edges into a group meet the painted border
%% instead of ending inside it, and the frame is not widened after the fact.
flowchart LR
  org[Org]
  subgraph platform["Platform and infrastructure services"]
    infra[infra]
  end
  subgraph product["Product experience and onboarding"]
    app[app]
  end
  subgraph shared["Shared design system and tokens"]
    design[design]
    icons[icons]
  end
  org --> platform
  org --> product
  org --> shared
  app --> infra
  design --> app
